      "writtenOn": "2026-11-26T05:49:24Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Falling back to `Session::new_for_testing()` in production code when `root_path_` or `build_dir_` is unset feels risky: `PathResolver::new_for_testing()` hardcodes compile-time test paths (`CARGO_MANIFEST_DIR/...`), so an accidental call before setup finishes would silently use test paths instead of failing loudly.\n\nIf this fallback is mainly to avoid breaking non-Starlark unit tests (where `TestWithScope::CreateBuildSettingsForTest()` sets `build_dir_` without `root_path_`) when writers call `starlark_session()`, keeping the initialized check in the writers should make this fallback unnecessary. Then we could assert `DCHECK(!root_path_.empty() \u0026\u0026 !build_dir_.is_null())` here (and have Starlark tests configure `root_path_` explicitly if needed).",
      "isAi": true,
      "revId": "01416fbe32bdcb4df9cbd5589f7e399e47cdc175",
      "serverId": "c360c8e5-7aa8-3905-a7a0-810934766dac"
