      "side": 1,
      "message": "Optional suggestion: instead of lock-free CAS initialization here, would double-checked locking (`std::atomic\u003cSession*\u003e` + `std::mutex` taken only on the slow path) be preferable?\n\nWith CAS, if multiple worker threads hit `load()` concurrently before initialization, each thread constructs a full `Session` (building `Globals` and preloading builtins) and discards the losing ones. DCLP keeps the exact same lock-free `acquire` load fast path (and keeps `has_starlark_session()` / `starlark_session_if_initialized()` thread-safe without pulling `\"cxx.h\"` back into `build_settings.h`), while guaranteeing `Session` is only constructed once. Since there is typically only one `BuildSettings` instance per build, the extra `std::mutex` member size should be negligible.",
      "isAi": true,
      "revId": "01416fbe32bdcb4df9cbd5589f7e399e47cdc175",
      "serverId": "c360c8e5-7aa8-3905-a7a0-810934766dac"
    },
