      "writtenOn": "2026-11-26T05:49:24Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Removing the `has_starlark_session()` guard here (and at line 368 / `json_project_writer.cc:378`) means even builds that never use Starlark will eagerly construct a full `Session` (including building `Globals` and preloading builtins) during output writing just to query empty rules/loaded files and immediately drop it.\n\nThat seems to defeat the main benefit of lazy initialization for non-Starlark builds. Could we keep `has_starlark_session()` (e.g., `starlark_session_.load(std::memory_order_acquire) !\u003d nullptr`) or add a non-initializing accessor like `const Session* starlark_session_if_initialized() const` so these read-only writers skip initialization when unused?",
      "isAi": true,
      "revId": "01416fbe32bdcb4df9cbd5589f7e399e47cdc175",
      "serverId": "c360c8e5-7aa8-3905-a7a0-810934766dac"
    },
